<title>USA: AC-Pacific Intertie maintenance planned Mar 1-2.</title>
<headline>AC-Pacific Intertie maintenance planned Mar 1-2.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southbound power flows on the AC Pacific Intertie, which runs between the Northwest and California, will be reduced on March 1 and 2 for maintenance, the Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) said Friday.</p>
<p>Transmission capacity will be limited to 2,800 megawatts (MW), compared with an existing rate of 3,200 MW, between 0730 and 2400 PST on that weekend, a BPA spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
</text>
